        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**The available peer audit identifies an event created 75 minutes after September entered Pending Close. Its recorded `POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented treatment for this type of new transaction.** The event details remain subject to direct source-record confirmation, as noted below.\n\n### Identified activity\n\n| Field | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Cost event | **CE-250904-0004** |\n| Event type | `INPUT` — component issue |\n| Amount | **USD 284,763.42** — 28,476,342 cents |\n| Event-created time | **2025-09-30T19:15:00** |\n| September Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Recorded accounting status | **`POSTED`** |\n\nThe timestamps are reproduced exactly as supplied; no timezone offset was provided.\n\n**Lateness:** `19:15:00 − 18:00:00 = 4,500 seconds = 75 minutes`—one hour and 15 minutes after Pending Close.\n\n### Oracle policy assessment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting”** (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that new transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing.\n\nThe documented exceptions are **revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments**. The identified component-issue `INPUT` event is not one of those exceptions. Therefore, **on the reported event facts, `POSTED` is not consistent with the supplied Pending Close policy**.\n\n### Evidence qualification\n\nI directly verified the work order, September Pending Close timestamp, and Oracle policy. The event’s transaction ID, amount, creation time, type, and status came from an accessible peer analyst’s audit report—not a direct read of the restricted supporting event record. The submitted review therefore remains **“needs evidence”**, pending direct event-record confirmation.\n\nThe review was read-only; **no database records were changed**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
